message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Nilpotent-free spaces of 3 x 3 matrices over the field with three elements"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bhattacharjee
    given-names: Deep
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0466-750X"
    affiliation: "Formerly, Electro-Gravitational Space Propulsion Laboratory (EGSPL), Bhubaneswar, Odisha 751030, India"
    email: d.bhattacharjee@erl-forschung.de
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-13
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/creelie/congenial-waddle"
keywords:
  - nilpotent matrices
  - spaces of matrices
  - finite fields
  - Gerstenhaber's theorem
  - Lean 4
abstract: >-
  Wigderson conjectured that for every finite field F and every n there is a space of n x n
  matrices over F of dimension n^2 - binom(n,2) whose only nilpotent element is zero. Every
  six-dimensional space of 3 x 3 matrices over F_3 contains a nonzero nilpotent matrix, so the
  conjecture fails for F = F_3 and n = 3; the largest possible dimension is five. The proof is
  formalised in Lean 4 with Mathlib.
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Duality for matrix space questions"
    authors:
      - family-names: Wigderson
        given-names: Yuval
